# Raphael, Ninja Destroyer: "Until end of turn, you don't lose this mana as steps and phases end." That effect is an "until
# end of turn" effect, which ends in the cleanup step's second action (CR 514.2); the mana then empties as that cleanup step
# ends (CR 500.5), even when players had priority in it and another cleanup step follows (CR 514.3a). Turn 8, Bot2's: Bot1
# Shocks its own Raphael for {R}{R}. In the cleanup step Bot2 discards to hand size, which triggers its Marauding Mako, so
# players get priority and the mana is still in Bot1's pool; Bot2 casts Ancestral Recall, so the next cleanup step discards
# again and Mako triggers again. In that second cleanup step Bot1's pool is empty.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Ruby
Raphael, Ninja Destroyer
Mountain
Shock
Mountain x15

[Bot2 Deck]
Mountain
Mox Sapphire
Marauding Mako
Ancestral Recall
Island x16

